NAME
       umount - detach a file system from the directory tree

SYNOPSIS
       umount [-lf] TARGET...

DESCRIPTION
       Detach the mount at each TARGET from the mount namespace of the
       calling process. TARGET must be a mount point. Requires root.

       Without -l, umount fails with "Device or resource busy" when a file
       on the mount is open, or when other mounts exist below it. The
       directory of a process is not checked.

OPTIONS
       -l, --lazy
           remove the mount, and every mount below it, from the namespace
           at once. Open files keep working; the file system is released
           when the last one is closed

       -f, --force
           accepted and ignored

SEE ALSO
       mount(8), unshare(1)
